<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.884 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.884 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.7 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due May 22, 1997 was 2.884 percent, up from 2.842 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.2 billion of 175-day T-bills due August 14, 1997 was 3.103 percent, down from 3.133 percent last week, and on C$1.2 billion of 364-day T-bills due February 19, 1998 was 3.425 percent, down from 3.444 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$525 million three-month, C$125 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$875 million of C$5.8 billion bills due Feb 27.</p>
